diagnosis_text:
Scope and component: The “gateway boxes” for both floors are the Layer‑3 SVI gateways hosted on device sshswitch: br_v5 (10.5.0.254/24) for VLAN 5 and br_v6 (10.6.0.254/24) for VLAN 6. Mechanism: End hosts in 10.5.0.x and 10.6.0.x ARP for their default gateway and send to sshswitch via the VLAN-tagged trunk on ms1_sw4 (eth0.5/eth0.6 on both sshswitch and switch4). Localization evidence: On sshswitch, br_v5 and br_v6 are UP with IPs 10.5.0.254 and 10.6.0.254, and the trunk subinterfaces eth0.5/eth0.6 are bridged correctly. From pcs: pc1 (10.5.0.1) and pc2 (10.5.0.2) both ping 10.5.0.254 successfully; pc3 (10.6.0.3) and pc4 (10.6.0.4) both ping 10.6.0.254 successfully. ARP on hosts resolves the gateway MAC to 4e:44:66:e5:55:8e, which matches sshswitch’s bridge MAC. sshswitch can also ping these hosts. Root cause: No current fault is present; both gateway SVIs are up and reachable, so the earlier reported outage is not reproducible now. Corrective fix: None required at this time. If the issue reappears after reloads, ensure sshswitch’s network configuration persists (bond0, eth0.5/eth0.6, and bridges br_v5/br_v6 with 10.5.0.254/10.6.0.254) and that ms1_sw4 remains a VLAN trunk; consider enabling a startup check/monitor to verify the bridges and VLAN subinterfaces come up after reboots.
=== END ===